Things to note here:

  - Menu is generated randomly: 11 types of food of monster not unique and
   not genocided + 4 random potions.
  - As you expect from a good restaurant, it is REALLY expensive.
  - New objects have been added: mousses, pates, etc... They are expensive
   only in restaurants, to prevent user selling food back to normal shops.
  - The code for the chef is the same that for a shopkeeper (digging, kops,
   teleporting away, etc...)
  - The service costs you 100 $.
  - Cannot sell objects in a restaurant, even food objects.
  - If you kill the chef, you get all the menu for free.
  - When you have got an item from the menu, it dissapears from it.If someone
   gets them all, when sitting at the table, the chef answers:

    "Sorry, I've nothing cooked right now." or
    "Sorry, but my cellar is currently empty"

  - Eating one of these new delicatessen gives the same random probability of
   getting the correspondent intrinsic as a normal corpse, but if the monster
   is poisonous or deadly, you only get the message:

    "Uf! Strong stuff!"

    and lose some hit points. You don't have any restaurants in your country 
    that are allowed to poison customers, do you?   :-)

  - All of these is already implemented, now under beta-testing.
  - What should be the possibilities of such a room compared to others?
   What levels? Should be a bit cheaper? Any other features?
   Some good names for chefs? (right now I have only Maxim, Paul Bocuse & 
			     Michelin + some spanish ones).

  - Please let me know of any spelling/grammar error, specially in the french
   part.


